 Mar 2004. URL: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.emedicine.com/med/topic3514.htm"/></comment></citation></ref><ref id="b16"><citation citation-type="web"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Brook</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Lucey</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Gunn</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Intramuscular ziprasidone compared with intramuscular haloperidol in the treatment of acute psychosis</article-title><source>J Clin Psychiatry</source><year>2000</year><volume>61</volume><fpage>933</fpage><lpage>41</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11206599</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b17"><citation citation-type="confproc"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Brook</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Walden</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Benattia</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Ziprasidone versus haloperidol in sequential IM/oral treatment of acute schizophrenia</article-title><year>2001</year><conf-name>Poster presented at the American College of Neuropsychopharmacology (ACNP) 40th Annual Meeting</conf-name><conf-date>2001 Dec 9&#x02013;13</conf-date><conf-loc>Waikoloa, HI, USA</conf-loc></citation></ref><ref id="b18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Brown</surname><given-names>DW</given-names></name><name><surname>Giles</surname><given-names>WH</given-names></name><name><surname>Greenlund</surname><given-names>KJ</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Impaired fasting glucose, diabetes mellitus, and cardiovascular disease risk factors are associated with prolonged QTc duration. Results from the Third National Health and Nutrition Examination Survey</article-title><source>J Cardiovasc Risk</source><year>2001</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>227</